## Description

A personal portfolio website built with pure HTML5, CSS3, and vanilla JavaScript
(no frameworks, no libraries, no backend). The site uses a pastel "folder-card"
visual theme — projects are presented as colorful folders you click to open,
matching the idea of "ideas and progress tucked inside a folder."

The portfolio includes a hero introduction, an About Me section, a projects
section with two clickable project cards that link to full detail pages, and
a contact form with client-side validation.

## Features

- Pastel folder-card design system (pink, green, yellow, blue, purple, orange)
- Rounded cards, folder tabs, soft shadows, and italic section labels
- Fully responsive layout for desktop, tablet, and mobile (CSS Grid + Flexbox)
- Dark / light mode toggle with the choice saved in `localStorage`
- Smooth scrolling for in-page navigation links
- Two dedicated project detail pages with overview, key features, tools, and
  personal contribution
- Contact form with required-field validation and a success message on submit
  (no backend — handled entirely in JavaScript)

